.TITLE "du"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Estimates file space usage on macOS. This command displays the disk usage of
files and directories within a specified path. It helps in identifying which
files or folders are consuming the most disk space, making it valuable for
__disk space management__ and cleanup.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**diskusage**

.DIV "TLDR"
**du -h __/path/to/directory__**
Displays the disk usage of a __/path/to/directory__ in human-readable format.
> __-h__: human-readable flag | __/path/to/directory__: The path to the directory to inspect.

**du -sh __/path/to/directory__**
Displays the total size of a __/path/to/directory__ in human-readable format.
> __-s__: summarize total size flag | __-h__: human-readable flag | __/path/to/directory__: The path to the directory.

**du -a -h**
Displays disk usage for all files and directories in the current path in human-readable format.
> __-a__: all files and directories flag | __-h__: human-readable flag

**du -d 1 -h __/path/to/directory__**
Displays disk usage for __/path/to/directory__ and its immediate subdirectories (depth 1).
> __-d 1__: depth level 1 flag | __-h__: human-readable flag | __/path/to/directory__: The path to the directory.

.DIV "SUMMARY"
`du` is particularly useful for tracking down large files or directories
that are consuming excessive disk space. Combining it with `sort -rh` and
`head` can help quickly identify the largest offenders (e.g., `du -sh * | sort -rh | head`).

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:df** **mac:ls**

documentation: https://ss64.com/osx/du.html
